{"id": "EUVD-2026-105088", "enisaUuid": "e0185d34-168c-30f6-9bb4-d535ce648dbf", "description": "Xen Orchestra before 6.9.0 contains an authorization bypass vulnerability in the xo-server user.set API method that allows low-privileged authenticated users to modify other users' preferences by supplying an arbitrary target user id. Attackers can delete the preferences.otp TOTP secret to disable two-factor authentication, corrupt it to block logins, or overwrite stored xsCredentials and sshKeys.", "datePublished": "2026-10-20T15:40:35", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20T18:19:50", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/vatesfr/xen-orchestra/security/advisories/GHSA-mc4m-hc98-rhmv", "https://github.com/vatesfr/xen-orchestra/commit/3dbf8738f1e682b96ade2074dc84bee02a0c2d48", "https://github.com/vatesfr/xen-orchestra/blob/f187b7931988e3e5c9ccd58abe730d6b006cc246/packages/xo-server/src/api/user.mjs#L73-L93", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/xen-orchestra-before-6.9.0-authorization-bypass-via-user-set-api"], "aliases": ["GHSA-22x8-669x-gh7m", "CVE-2026-113610"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.43, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "69361a7e-25a1-336c-b0d6-1a3eba505112", "product": {"name": "xen-orchestra", "vendor": {"name": "vatesfr"}}, "product_version": "0 <6.9.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "f540c6b7-e246-3045-a89f-17b3793b0a55", "vendor": {"name": "vatesfr"}}], "isExploited": false}